@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction — LayerZero.Tools.Web";
}

<div class="docs-wrapper">
    <aside class="docs-sidebar">
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_DocsSidebar")
    </aside>

    <div class="docs-content">
        <h1>LayerZero.Tools.Web</h1>
        <p class="page-subtitle">Convention-based asset bundling for ASP.NET Core — zero config, zero external framework.</p>

        <h2>What is it?</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>LayerZero.Tools.Web</strong> is a self-contained CSS and JavaScript bundling system for .NET 8+.
            It automatically discovers and serves bundles based on your controller/action folder structure — no manual
            asset registration, no WebPack, no WebOptimizer required.
        </p>
        <p>
            Bundles are built lazily on first request, cached in memory, and served by a built-in middleware with
            correct <code>ETag</code> and <code>Cache-Control</code> headers. A file-system watcher evicts stale cache
            entries the moment a source file changes.
        </p>

        <h2>Key Features</h2>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> Convention-over-configuration discovery</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> Controller &amp; action bundle granularity</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> Inline critical CSS &amp; JS</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> NUglify minification + validation</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> ETag / 304 Not Modified support</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> Content-hash cache-busting URLs</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> File-watcher cache eviction</div>
            <div class="feature-item"><span class="fi-icon">✅</span> Zero external framework dependencies</div>
        </div>

        <h2>Folder Convention</h2>
        <p>Drop files in the right folder and bundles are auto-generated. No manual registration needed.</p>
        <div class="folder-tree">
<span class="ft-dim">wwwroot/</span>
<span class="ft-dim">├── </span><span class="ft-dir">css/</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   ├── </span><span class="ft-dir">Controller/</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   │   └── </span><span class="ft-dir">Home/</span><span class="ft-dim">          ← controller bundle</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   │       ├── </span><span class="ft-file">Home.css</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   │       └── </span><span class="ft-dir">Index/</span><span class="ft-dim">         ← action bundle</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   │           └── </span><span class="ft-file">StyleSheet.css</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   ├── </span><span class="ft-dir">Common/</span><span class="ft-dim">            ← shared across all pages</span>
<span class="ft-dim">│   └── </span><span class="ft-dir">critical/</span><span class="ft-dim">          ← inlined before everything</span>
<span class="ft-dim">└── </span><span class="ft-dir">js/</span><span class="ft-dim">                     ← mirrors css/ structure</span>
        </div>

        <h2>How Bundles are Served</h2>
        <p>When a page is rendered, the TagHelpers emit <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags for any bundles
        that match the current controller/action. The bundle URLs are served by <code>BundleServingMiddleware</code>.</p>
        <pre class="docs-code"><span class="cm">/* Requesting /Home/Index emits: */</span>
&lt;style&gt;<span class="cm">/* critical CSS inlined */</span>&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="<span class="str">/bundles/home.min.css</span>" /&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="<span class="str">/bundles/home/index.min.css</span>" /&gt;

&lt;script&gt;<span class="cm">/* critical JS inlined */</span>&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="<span class="str">/bundles/home.min.js</span>"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="<span class="str">/bundles/home/index.min.js</span>"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</pre>

        <h2>Dependencies</h2>
        <p>Your application only needs:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>NUglify</strong> — bundled, handles CSS/JS minification and validation</li>
            <li><strong>Microsoft.AspNetCore.App</strong> — standard framework reference</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout callout-tip">
            <strong>No WebOptimizer required.</strong>
            Previous versions depended on <code>LigerShark.WebOptimizer.Core</code>, <code>AngleSharp.Css</code>, and <code>Esprima</code>.
            All three were removed in v2.1.0. LayerZero.Tools.Web is now fully self-contained.
        </div>

        <h2>Current Version</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>v2.1.0</strong> — Self-contained, ETag-aware, file-watcher cache eviction, unified BundleStore pipeline for all asset types including critical CSS/JS.
            See the <a asp-controller="Docs" asp-action="ChangeLogs">Changelog</a> for full history.
        </p>

        <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem; display:flex; gap: 1rem;">
            <a asp-controller="Docs" asp-action="Setup" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Get Started →</a>
            <a asp-controller="Docs" asp-action="ChangeLogs" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm">Changelog</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
